<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39599" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pūnītor</span></b> ,
		ōris, m.
		punio. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A punisher</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">seditiosorum punitor acerrimus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 67</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Val.
				Max. 6, 1, 8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An avenger</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fuit ultor injuriae, punitor doloris sui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Mil. 13, 35</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Crassianae stragis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 3, 4, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
